{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261112T181205Z_dev-04_staged_b33b", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "For the 4b on-shell cascade, the AMS-02 antiproton limits approach or intersect the GCE-preferred regions at the smaller mass ratios, r = 0.2–0.4. At the larger ratios shown (up to r = 1.0, with panels at r = 0.2, 0.3, …, 1.0), the antiproton limits stay above the GCE-preferred regions, so they do not constrain them. I read this from the paper's text; I did not see the figure itself. The r = 0.1 fits are much poorer and are not shown.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.3"}]}, "turns": 11, "seconds": 20.056, "tool_calls": 10, "tool_result_chars": 51726, "input_tokens": 187899, "output_tokens": 982, "parser_versions": ["3"], "ended_at": "2026-11-12T18:12:25+00:00"}
